Changes code from Helium's helium/core/translate/provider-api.patch (GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors).

Helium 0.22 adds an API for translation providers (the HeliumTranslate feature, off by default): a registered
provider is sent the text of the page to translate, on the device or over the network. No provider is registered in
this tree. Ray has no translation feature in the base browser, so HasTranslationProvider is false whatever the
feature says or a later Helium registers: Chrome's Translate menu items, bubble and settings section stay hidden and
no page text leaves the renderer. The provider code stays and compiles.

--- a/components/translate/core/browser/translation_provider.cc
+++ b/components/translate/core/browser/translation_provider.cc
@@ -109,8 +109,7 @@
 }
 
 bool HasTranslationProvider() {
-  return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kHeliumTranslate) &&
-         !GetProviders().empty();
+  return false;
 }
 
 TranslationProvider* GetTranslationProvider() {
